    "## 3. Modeling Schemes Comparison\n",
    "We will test 3 different schemes ensuring variations in Algorithm, Feature Extraction, and Data Split.\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Scheme 1:** SVM + TF-IDF (80/20 Split)\n",
    "2. **Scheme 2:** Random Forest + CountVectorizer (80/20 Split)\n",
    "3. **Scheme 3:** Bi-LSTM + Embedding (70/30 Split) -> **Target > 92% Acc**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "scheme1_md",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Scheme 1: SVM + TF-IDF (80/20)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "scheme1_code",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Split Data 80/20\n",
    "X_train_80, X_test_20, y_train_80, y_test_20 = train_test_split(\n",
    "    df_clean['cleaned_text'], df_clean['label'], test_size=0.2, random_state=42, stratify=df_clean['label']\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Pipeline: TF-IDF -> SVM\n",
    "pipeline_svm = make_pipeline(TfidfVectorizer(), SVC(kernel='linear', C=1.0, probability=True))\n",
    "pipeline_svm.fit(X_train_80, y_train_80)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Verify Accuracy\n",
    "y_pred_svm = pipeline_svm.predict(X_test_20)\n",
    "acc_svm = accuracy_score(y_test_20, y_pred_svm)\n",
    "print(f\"Scheme 1 (SVM) Accuracy: {acc_svm:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(classification_report(y_test_20, y_pred_svm, target_names=['Negative', 'Positive', 'Spam']))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "scheme2_md",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Scheme 2: Random Forest + CountVectorizer (80/20)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "scheme2_code",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Pipeline: CountVectorizer -> Random Forest\n",
    "# Using the same 80/20 split as Scheme 1 but different Features and Algo\n",
    "pipeline_rf = make_pipeline(CountVectorizer(), RandomForestClassifier(n_estimators=100, random_state=42))\n",
    "pipeline_rf.fit(X_train_80, y_train_80)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Verify Accuracy\n",
    "y_pred_rf = pipeline_rf.predict(X_test_20)\n",
    "acc_rf = accuracy_score(y_test_20, y_pred_rf)\n",
    "print(f\"Scheme 2 (Random Forest) Accuracy: {acc_rf:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(classification_report(y_test_20, y_pred_rf, target_names=['Negative', 'Positive', 'Spam']))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "scheme3_md",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Scheme 3: Deep Learning (Bi-LSTM) (70/30 Split)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "dl_prep",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "VOCAB_SIZE = 5000\n",
    "MAX_LENGTH = 100\n",
    "EMBEDDING_DIM = 64\n",
    "\n",
    "tokenizer = Tokenizer(num_words=VOCAB_SIZE, oov_token=\"<OOV>\")\n",
    "tokenizer.fit_on_texts(df_clean['cleaned_text'])\n",
    "\n",
    "sequences = tokenizer.texts_to_sequences(df_clean['cleaned_text'])\n",
    "padded_sequences = pad_sequences(sequences, maxlen=MAX_LENGTH, padding='post', truncating='post')\n",
    "\n",
    "X_dl = padded_sequences\n",
    "y_dl = df_clean['label'].values\n",
    "\n",
    "# Split Data 70/30 (DIFFERENT SPLIT from Schemes 1 & 2)\n",
    "X_train_dl, X_test_dl, y_train_dl, y_test_dl = train_test_split(X_dl, y_dl, test_size=0.3, random_state=42, stratify=y_dl)\n",
    "print(f\"DL Train shape: {X_train_dl.shape}, Test shape: {X_test_dl.shape}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "dl_model",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "model = Sequential([\n",
    "    Embedding(VOCAB_SIZE, EMBEDDING_DIM, input_length=MAX_LENGTH),\n",
    "    SpatialDropout1D(0.3),\n",
    "    Bidirectional(LSTM(128, return_sequences=True)),\n",
    "    Dropout(0.4),\n",
    "    Bidirectional(LSTM(64)),\n",
    "    Dense(64, activation='relu'),\n",
    "    Dropout(0.4),\n",
    "    Dense(3, activation='softmax') # 3 Output Classes\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "model.compile(loss='sparse_categorical_crossentropy', optimizer='adam', metrics=['accuracy'])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Callbacks\n",
    "checkpoint = ModelCheckpoint(\"best_model.keras\", monitor='val_accuracy', verbose=1, save_best_only=True, mode='max')\n",
    "early_stop = EarlyStopping(monitor='val_loss', patience=5, restore_best_weights=True)\n",
    "reduce_lr = ReduceLROnPlateau(factor=0.5, patience=2, min_lr=1e-6)\n",
    "\n",
    "history = model.fit(\n",
    "    X_train_dl, y_train_dl,\n",
    "    epochs=20,\n",
    "    batch_size=32,\n",
    "    validation_data=(X_test_dl, y_test_dl),\n",
    "    callbacks=[checkpoint, early_stop, reduce_lr]\n",
    ")"
   ]
